# VitalPet — Project Context

## What this product is
VitalPet is a **Flutter** mobile app (iOS 16+ / Android 10+) that turns daily symptom logging into a habit using a virtual pet companion. Users check in daily; the pet thrives or dies based on consistency. An on-device SLM sequences follow-up questions based on the user's symptom history. A doctor-facing PDF handoff is generated entirely offline using pure Dart. There is no backend server. All data lives on the device, AES-256 encrypted.

## Tech stack (exact packages)
- **Framework**: Flutter 3.x, Dart (Impeller renderer, 60/120fps)
- **Platform**: iOS 16+ primary. Android is post-hackathon — do not write Android-specific code unless explicitly instructed.
- **State management**: Riverpod 3.x (`flutter_riverpod`, `riverpod_annotation`)
- **Navigation**: go_router 14.x
- **Local DB**: drift 2.x (type-safe SQLite ORM) + `sqlcipher_flutter_libs` (AES-256 encryption)
- **SLM inference**: `flutter_gemma` → MediaPipe LLM Inference API on-device (Gemma 3n E2B int4)
- **Animations**: Flutter built-in AnimatedBuilder + Tween (pet rocking/bounce effect,
  PNG swap per vitality state) + `confetti` 0.7.x (milestone streaks). No Rive dependency.
- **Health integration**: `health` 12.x (unified HealthKit + Health Connect adapter)
- **PDF generation**: `pdf` 3.x + `printing` 5.x (pure Dart, zero native bridge required)
- **Notifications**: `flutter_local_notifications` 18.x
- **Widgets**: WidgetKit Swift (iOS) + Glance Kotlin (Android) — both **mandatory native**, not Flutter
- **Testing**: `flutter_test` + `mocktail` + `integration_test`

